Job Description
Sylvania is looking for a Technical Manager to assist with optimising process efficiencies on existing plants, for implementing production reporting and metal accounting best practices and systems, for design input and approval on behalf of the client to feasibility studies and engineering phases of new plant construction projects, to provide support for implementing new technology identified through R&D (output of R&D projects managed by R&D Manager) and providing technical process support to the operations.
Key Responsibilities:
Optimise and align plant operating and control philosophy;
Audit of current operating and control philosophy against policy; gap analysis; guidelines to plants for aligning with requirements;
Initial and periodic audits of metal accounting systems;
Optimise the use of reagents and grinding media;
Management of process test work aimed at trouble shooting process inefficiencies;
Support of R&D project test work and design integration for projects aimed at improving concentrator efficiencies;
Monitor and benchmark economic drivers for plant performance;
Identification of opportunities to improve process stability;
Participate in process optimisation projects; approve and sign off design changes for implementing brown fields process changes aimed at optimising process efficiencies;
Implement production reporting system and data trend analysis tools required for
identification, trouble shooting and optimising process inefficiencies;
Respond to data supporting process changes to initiate improvement process;
Benchmarking of plant performance through data analysis;
Collaborate with Group Engineering Manager to Optimise plant availability;
Assist with evaluation of plant asset performance and motivations for replacement / improvement of production assets;
Assist Group Engineering Manager with roll-out of systems to measure plant availability;
Reviews and approves process design and specifications for improvement projects and new projects as part of existing metals portfolio;
Provides input to process design for new metals portfolio;
Providing technical support to processing operations;
Co-ordination of process test work and studies aimed at motivating business improvement projects for existing operations;
Manage and direct output of Senior Metallurgists;
Technical and process input to design of projects aimed at improving plant efficiencies and concentrate quality.
Knowledge / Education Requirement:
B.Sc. (or B.Eng) Chemical Engineering, or chemistry degree Project Management or related qualification would be advantageous;
5 to 7 years post qualification experience in mineral extraction processes,
3 years relevant experience in comminution and flotation.
Diverse experience in metallurgy and recovery of metalliferous minerals would be beneficial
Excellent written and verbal communication skills;
Computer literacy, excellent Excel, database and presentation skills;
Must have a valid code 8 driver’s license and be willing to travel frequently;
Must be in possession of a valid certificate of fitness;

Description
Ground Operations, Hub & Gateway Operations, including but not limited to:
Contract Management/ Sourcing; Customer Service;
Dispatch; Domestic Special Services;
GSP Management;
NNP Management;
Handling;
Network Control;
On Road; Quality Management;
Service Assurance; Transport Scheduling;
Clearance & Brokerage Operations;
Clearance Admin Inbound/ Outbound;
Clearance Regulatory;
Commercial Airline Management, Spot Management, Lift;
Cross-border Linehaul;
Dangerous Goods; Export Controls; Hub Control Centre; Vendor Management;
Weight & Balance (Ramp Operations)
Qualifications
:
Degree level qualifications or equivalent experience. Job specific qualifications desirable.
Experience and Skills:
Extensive work-related skill, knowledge or experience is required.
FedEx Management and/or International experience highly desirable.
Fluent in English, with other local language(s) desirable.
Other Duties:
Incumbent may be required to perform other duties as assigned.
Additional requirements or responsibilities may be detailed in other sources, including but not limited to policy and procedure manuals, standard operating plans, training manuals, specific functional or department rules, etc.
Process and Planning Responsibilities:
Develops strategies and tactics for area of responsibility, within remit.
Responsible for mid and long range (annual/2+years) planning and setting forward looking functional teams’ goals.
FedEx was built on a philosophy that puts people first, one we take seriously. We are an equal opportunity/affirmative action employer and we are committed to a diverse, equitable, and inclusive workforce in which we enforce fair treatment, and provide growth opportunities for everyone.
All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment regardless of age, race, color, national origin, genetics, religion, gender, marital status, pregnancy (including childbirth or a related medical condition), physical or mental disability, or any other characteristic protected by applicable laws, regulations, and ordinances.

Minimum Requirements
Grade 12
Bachelor of Pharmacy
Registered with the South African Pharmacy Council
Advanced Computer Literacy level in MS Word, Excel, PowerPoint and Outlook
Job Related Requirements
Minimum of 1 year experience in either Warehousing, Distribution or Production in the Pharmacy sector.
Locum experience within these sectors will be considered.
Compliance: Demonstrate Quality Lead support ensuring full site compliance, including but not limited to: ▪ DSV Policies (domestic and global), and Domestic authoritative statutory measures (eg. SAHPRA, DoL, etc.);
Training: Demonstrate Quality Lead support eQuality Management System (PharmaQMS) compliance; o Facilitate the necessary training of employees (operations, sales, HR and IT) inclusive of on-site contractors
Consumer / Retail product management: o Health product identification and compliant storage, with segregation by resultant UN Code and/or MSDS category. This to be done collaboratively with DSV Quality / Compliance Department;
Problem Solving: Effective Root Cause Analysis, Trend Analysis, Problem Solving and implementation of Corrective and Preventative Measures;
Auditing: o Ensure audit readiness aligned to DSV adopted Integrated Management system, adopted PharmaQMS as well as prescribed regulatory impositions. This inclusive of preparation, execution and reporting of mentioned audit scope;
Stress and Conflict: Effective techniques and/or skills to manage conflict, cope with stress and work under pressure to meet deadlines;
Communication: Communicate effectively (written and verbal) to manage and meet both internal and external customer expectations;
Willing to work night shift.
Contractor Management - Support Quality Lead with business partner reviews per annual developed plan. This focused on licenses, certifications, processes, staff, training and equipment; and related.nsuring ongoing Pharma
Added Advantages for this role
Ability to interpret pharmacy legislation;
Prepare and implement necessary policies, procedures and codes of practice; Ability to demonstrate a proactive approach and continuously develop pharmaceutical quality, and other related obligations;
An understanding of pharmaceutical production, whether largeor small-scale; and
An understanding of quality assurance and audit processes in relation to the pharmaceutical industry and associated quality management systems.
Main purpose of the role
The successful incumbent will be obligated to ensure adherence to statutory requirements as outlined in the Pharmacy Act 53/1974, Medicines and Related Substances Control Act 101/1965 and all associated regulations. Commitment to quality in respect of pharmaceutical product integrity remains pivotal. Further to the said, with the DSV business’ participation in the Global HealthcareQMS certification – a voluntary standard maintained by DSV’s Global Healthcare Compliance Department – the incumbent is required to portray a Pharmaceutical and Healthcare Quality Lead role, which endeavours to uphold the stated standard.
This particular portfolio is perceived as a part-time role mainly determined by the facility’s assigned tier and, therefore, its associated capabilities. Regardless of full or part-time consideration, commitment to quality in respect of pharmaceutical product integrity remains pivotal with the incumbent, per occasion, portraying the role of the delegated representative acting on behalf of the Responsible Pharmacist. This done in good faith and ensuring appeasement of regulatory authorities, whether domestic or foreign, as and when required.
Duties and Responsibilities
Assume responsibility for all compliance obligations set forth in the Pharmacy Act 53/1974, Medicines and Related Substances Act 101/1965 and associated regulations on behalf of the DSV Solutions’ business unit; Upholding GxP principles at the DSV Solutions Gauteng Park wholesale pharmacy;
Per occasion, act as deputy or delegated Responsible Pharmacist (RP) to the DSV Solutions Gauteng Park wholesale pharmacy as and when required by the appointed RP;
Co-ordinate repackaging of medicines, as and when required;
Co-ordinate the destruction of medicine according to client and regulatory requirements, as and when required;
Aid in remedying warehouse control and management system discrepancies;
Maintain the flow of product and ensure accurate record keeping;
Active participation in stock disposition decisions in respect of product damage(s), market returns, product recalls and product complaints (pharmacovigilance);
Active participation in procedures associated with product lifecycle i.e. receiving, sampling, retention and other;
Develop and implement operational processes, procedures, process flows and / or other written documentation in pursuit of pharmaceutical quality, as and when required;
Assist with audit undertaking whether internal or external audits, including but not limited to, procedure selfinspections, supplier, client and regulatory audits;
Active participation in CAPA process to ensure successful closure of identified shortcomings;
Support the maintenance of DSV’s central reporting repository in respect of DSV Solutions Gauteng Park SLA’s;
Data analysis, report execution and process improvement in support of solution development, implementation and operational excellence, as and when required;
Act as tutor to pharmacist assistants and be registered as such with the South African Pharmacy Council;
Provide assistance and apply knowledge, where needed, for general functions;
Review temperature monitoring equipment and related data, as and when required;
Active participation with facilities’ resources and infrastructure maintenance including but not limited to temperature probes, scale calibration and related; and
Close relations (including training & coaching) with Operational team members, Projects and Engineering, DSV Learning and Development department, business units and DSV clients in the development and implementation of customised solutions.
